# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Isaac J. Parker et al. (2026). False Metallization in Short-Ranged Machine Learned Interatomic Potentials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2603.04228  arXiv:2603.04228v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2603.04228v1 (sha256 f7fff47797574ecc...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 644 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/parker2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the short-ranged (SR) and long-ranged local-split-charge
# (LR) MACE models trained by the authors for a copper-water interface
# (Table S3; selected Table S8 variants) and for pure water on a published
# revPBE0-D3 data set (Table S5), with their validation RMSEs, and the
# MACE foundation models used as distributed. Dipole distributions, band
# gaps and the TiO2-water BPNNP analysis (models of Ref. 95) are
# property/analysis results.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
